reshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Tag the three matrix-comment ACs `[non-codebase]` and state the concrete on-ticket attestation (comment posted, with an enumerated row per named surface and a named missing-evidence field per UNKNOWN row) that constitutes 'done'.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["F1","E6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0072,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'classifies every row ... — checked by reading the comment'","'records the production-construction constraints ... — checked by reading the comment against the named sites'","'recorded UNKNOWN with the specific missing evidence named — checked by reading the matrix comment'","The comment is a ticket artifact, not a repo artifact, and no deterministic command produces evidence for these three ACs."],"finding":"The matrix-comment acceptance criteria are verified by human reading ('checked by reading the comment') rather than a deterministic in-session command, and they are not tagged [non-codebase] even though their 'done' evidence inherently lives on the ticket as prose. This leaves their classification/verification protocol under-specified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f85b1337b0cc9df75","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — bullets 1, 2, and 5 (capability-matrix comment, production-construction constraints, UNKNOWN evidence)","norm_id":"n88058e6802d23f99","priority":0.6072,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer/executor needs to confirm the matrix comment is complete but has only 'read it' as the check, with no enumerated row-count or required-field structure to assert against."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Prefix the comment-based ACs with `[non-codebase]` and specify the required structure (one classified row per the 11 named surfaces, each with a cited source; each UNKNOWN row names its missing evidence) so the read is checked